title: CompanionMeeting
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Companion runs up to hero at the Heartwood tree
<<wait 1.5>>
<<camera_focus companion>>

{$companionName}: Hey — you're the one the Heartwood called?
{$companionName}: Good. We need you.

-> What's happening here?
    {$companionName}: Short version? Elarion is under siege. Creatures from the wilds have been hitting our walls every night.
    {$companionName}: The Heartwood — that tree behind you — it's the only thing keeping this village standing. If it falls, we lose everything.
-> Who are you?
    {$companionName}: I'm {$companionName}. I've been holding things together here, but I can't do it alone.
    {$companionName}: The Heartwood called you for a reason. Let's find out what you can do.
-> I'm ready. Show me.
    {$companionName}: I like that. No questions, just action. We'll get along fine.

{$companionName}: Come on — I'll show you around. Stay close.
<<set $tutorialPhase to "tour">>
<<start_autowalk village_tour>>
===

title: VillageTour
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Walking through village — companion narrates buildings
<<wait 2>>

{$companionName}: This is Elarion. Small, but it's ours.

// Pass the Forge
<<camera_glance forge>>
{$companionName}: That's the Forge. Our Blacksmith can reinforce weapons and armor — yours included, once you've proven yourself.

// Pass the Arcane Tower
<<camera_glance arcane_tower>>
{$companionName}: The Arcane Tower. If you've got magic in you, that's where you sharpen it.

// Pass the Pet House
<<camera_glance pet_house>>
{$companionName}: And the Pet House. The wild Echoes — spirit animals — sometimes wander in. If you earn their trust, they'll fight for you. Or gather for you. Your call.

// Pass the Market
<<camera_glance market>>
{$companionName}: Market square. Trade, supplies, the occasional rare find.

{$companionName}: But none of this matters if the walls fall. Come on — this way.
<<start_autowalk gate_1>>
===

title: FirstTower
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Arrived at Gate 1
<<camera_focus gate_1>>
<<stop_autowalk>>

{$companionName}: See this gate? Last attack came right through here.
{$companionName}: We need eyes on it. A watchtower — something to slow them down.

// Teach tower placement
{$companionName}: Hit that Build button. I've got enough materials for one tower — place it near the gate.

<<highlight_ui build_button>>
<<set $tutorialStep to "place_first_tower">>
<<enable_player_input>>

// Wait for player to place tower
<<wait_for_event tower_placed>>

<<unhighlight_ui build_button>>
{$companionName}: Nice work. That'll buy us time when they come.
{$companionName}: But one tower won't hold four gates. Let's check the others.

<<set $towersBuilt to 1>>
<<start_autowalk gate_2>>
===

title: SecondGateAmbush
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Arrived at Gate 2
<<camera_focus gate_2>>
<<stop_autowalk>>

{$companionName}: We should put one here too...
<<wait 1>>
{$companionName}: Hmm. Not enough materials. We'll need to gather more before—

// HORN BLAST
<<play_sfx horn_warning>>
<<camera_shake 0.3>>
<<wait 0.5>>

{$companionName}: They're here. Defend this gate — NOW!

<<spawn_wave_at_nearest 3>>
<<set $tutorialStep to "first_combat">>
<<enable_player_input>>

// Companion fights alongside player — AI handles combat
// Wait for wave clear
<<wait_for_event wave_cleared>>

<<play_sfx victory_sting>>
<<wait 1>>

{$companionName}: We held them.
{$companionName}: Thanks for the help pushing them back.

<<wait 0.5>>

{$companionName}: But they'll be back. And next time it won't be three of them.

===

title: ResourceGrant
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Companion hands over supplies
{$companionName}: Here — I've been saving these. Take them.

<<grant_resources_for_towers 3>>
<<play_sfx resource_pickup>>

{$companionName}: That's enough to build a watchtower at each of the other three gates.
{$companionName}: Get them up before the next wave hits. Four gates, four towers — that's the minimum.

<<set $tutorialStep to "build_remaining">>
<<set_hud_objective "Build towers at the remaining 3 gates" 0 3>>
===

title: QuestCallout
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Companion points at quest panel
<<wait 1>>
<<highlight_ui quest_panel>>

{$companionName}: One more thing — see those tasks on the side?

-> What are those?
    {$companionName}: Jobs that need doing. Build, defend, explore — each one pays out. Resources, experience, sometimes something rarer.
    {$companionName}: They change regularly, so check back.
-> Got it.
    {$companionName}: Good. Don't ignore them — the rewards add up.

<<unhighlight_ui quest_panel>>
===

title: PetIntroduction
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Pet runs up to hero
<<spawn_starting_pet>>
<<wait 2>>

{$companionName}: Well — looks like you've already caught someone's attention.

<<camera_focus pet>>

{$companionName}: That's an Echo. A spirit animal tied to the Heartwood's energy. They choose who they follow.

{$companionName}: This one's chosen you. What do you want to call them?

<<show_pet_name_prompt>>
<<wait_for_event pet_named>>

{$companionName}: {$petName}. Good name.

{$companionName}: Now — {$petName} can help in two ways.

-> What do you mean?
    {$companionName}: They can stay here and help defend the village when enemies attack. Extra teeth at the gates.
    {$companionName}: Or they can go out and gather supplies from resource nodes. Wood, stone, food — whatever's nearby.
    {$companionName}: Your call. You can always change it later at the Pet House.
-> Just tell me the options.
    {$companionName}: Defend the village or gather resources. Simple choice, big impact.

<<show_pet_role_choice>>
<<wait_for_event pet_role_chosen>>

<<if $petRole == "defend">>
    {$companionName}: {$petName} will hold the line. Smart.
    {$companionName}: But we're going to need more resources soon. There's wood, iron, and more out beyond the gates — worth exploring when you're ready.
    <<set_hud_hint "Explore beyond the gates to find resources">>
<<else>>
    {$companionName}: {$petName} will bring back what they find. Good instinct.
    <<send_pet_to_harvest>>
    {$companionName}: Keep your eyes open out there too. The best nodes are further from the village — and more dangerous.
<<endif>>

===

title: TutorialComplete
tags: tutorial onboarding
---
// Final beat — camera shows all 4 gates
<<camera_show_all_gates>>
<<wait 3>>

{$companionName}: North, South, East, West. They can come from any direction.

<<camera_return_to_hero>>

{$companionName}: Get those towers built. Gather what you can. And when the next wave hits — we hold the line together.

-> Let's do this.
    {$companionName}: That's the spirit.
-> Any other advice?
    {$companionName}: Stay close to the walls during attacks. Explore during the quiet. And don't forget about {$petName} — they're part of your team now.
    {$companionName}: Oh — and talk to the villagers. The Blacksmith, the merchants — they've got things you'll need.

{$companionName}: I'll be right here if you need me. Good luck, Defender.

<<set $tutorialComplete to true>>
<<enable_full_controls>>
<<save_game>>
===
